         "1. Definition: natural physical surroundings in which a plant or animal lives and flourishes.\n2. Vital provision 1: Food and nutritional resources.\n3. Vital provision 2: Clean water and atmospheric gases (oxygen/carbon dioxide).\n4. Vital provision 3: Shelter, microclimate, and protection from predators.\n5. Vital provision 4: Mating territory and safe nesting conditions for reproduction.\n6. Examples: camel in desert habitat; water lily in freshwater pond habitat.",
