         "Adaptation refers to inherited, permanent structural or behavioral traits that evolved over thousands of years to help a species survive in its habitat (e.g. camel's hump and padded feet); Acclimatisation refers to short-term, reversible physiological adjustments made by an individual organism over days or weeks to cope with sudden environmental changes (e.g. breathing faster at high mountain altitudes).",
         "Adaptations are heritable genetic modifications selected over evolutionary generations. Acclimatisation represents phenotypic plasticity within an individual's lifetime.",
