         "Non-living objects lack cellular architecture, autopoietic metabolism, genetic inheritance, and internal growth (intussusception). External growth by accretion is fundamentally distinct from biological growth.",
         "1. Deconstruct car claim: cars consume fuel (combustion), but lack living cellular protoplasm; they do not repair damage, excrete biological waste, grow in size, or reproduce baby cars.\n2. Deconstruct cloud claim: a cloud 'grows' by accretion (external condensation of airborne water droplets adhering to dust nuclei); living organisms grow from within (intussusception) via mitosis and protein synthesis.\n3. Cellular criterion: all living beings are composed of one or more membrane-bound cells containing DNA; cars and clouds have zero cells.\n4. Reproductive criterion: only living beings reproduce offspring of their own species through genetic transmission.\n5. Conclude: fulfilling 1 or 2 isolated traits mechanically does not satisfy the integrated criteria of biological life.",
